        "pubDate": "2026-08-03T16:56:35Z",
        "description": "Impact-generated crater rays are well-documented on the Moon, with most appearing as high-albedo streaks extending radially from a crater's center. On Mars, however, crater rays are significantly rarer and discernible only through thermal imaging due to their lower thermal inertia compared to surrou",
        "title_cn": "火星陨石坑射线的长度及其与月球寒点的关系"
      }
